Well, you obviously haven't had monsters shoot wands very well. Especially
wands of death. My current game would be totally over if I _didn't_ have my
SoR. Got double-teamed early on (when I had just made it to dung. level 15)
by two Grey Elves with death wands. I got hit three times, once it reflected
back into the shooter, the other ttwo times the bolt missed on rebound.
Then yet again later while waltzing through Gehennom's earlier levels, a
bone devil of all things was shooting a wand of death at me. 
Without a SoR I'd be dead four times. Would be five but had an ammy of
lifesaving at the time.
Sure, this kind of run just doesn't happen all the time, but the point is,
it _can_, so why be unprepared and possibly exterminated?

Sure, there comes a point when reflection becomes near-moot, as the
wandshots always miss, but until that point, dancing and prancing around
without one could be potentially fatal.

The fact that you haven't needed one is just an example of an exceptional
game being played, with some blazing bright luck going on.



